# clang-tidy for the C this repository owns. run by `make check-c-tidy` and by mix ci as
# check.c_tidy, over c_src/*.c and c_src/test/*.c, with the vendored sources and the ERTS headers
# passed as -isystem so that findings are attributed to our code and not to theirs.
#
# The set is deliberately about defects rather than taste. This project follows gumbo's style
# because patches and the files they patch should read the same way, so the readability-* family
# would argue with a decision already made and clang-format already enforces. What is enabled is
# the family that finds real mistakes in the code this project wrote last: implicit conversions,
# bitwise operations on signed operands, multiplications that widen after the fact.
Checks: >
  bugprone-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  performance-*,
  cert-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-multi-level-implicit-pointer-conversion,
  -bugprone-not-null-terminated-result,
  -readability-*,
  -clang-analyzer-optin.*,

# bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters: every accessor here takes (resource, index) and the whole
# point of the naming is which is which.
#
# bugprone-multi-level-implicit-pointer-conversion: the vendored vector API takes void*, so every
# GumboNode** handed to it is that conversion, and there is nothing to fix on our side.
#
# bugprone-not-null-terminated-result: what this library moves between the two sides is always a
# (pointer, length) pair — Erlang binaries and GumboStringPiece are both length-delimited — so a
# memcpy into one of them is the whole operation and there is no terminator to add. The check is
# written for C strings, which is the representation this project deliberately does not use.
#
# clang-analyzer-optin.*: an opt-in heuristic that flags any allocation whose size comes from the
# input. For a library whose subject is parsing input, that is the whole program, and for the two
# harnesses it flags they are allocating the documents they were asked to build.
#
# cert-err33-c: enabled. It is the check this work exists to be able to turn on: it found 47 sites
# where a NIF's return value was disregarded, among them the enif_make_map_from_arrays family, whose
# failure used to travel into a detail map as a term and come back to a caller as the integer 42. Every
# extractor now reports by status code with the term in an out parameter, every call site checks it, and
# the entry points turn a 0 into a badarg. The check reports nothing in the C that ships — and check-c-tidy
# upgrades warnings to errors, so that sentence is now enforced rather than observed: a finding here
# fails the build instead of printing into a log nobody reads.
#
# It is off for c_src/test/parity_dump.c and c_src/test/teardown_probe.c, by the case in the
# Makefile's check-c-tidy: both print diagnostics to stderr, where the return value of a fprintf has no
# action to take and no caller to inform. That is the one disregard this project can name, and it is
# named here rather than paid for with ninety-four casts.
